              </flipboard>
            </zone>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='32054' id='6' story-point-id='5' type-v2='text' w='33268' x='1280' y='39730'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Australia&apos;s away batting problem is an India problem — and specifically a spin problem.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>
Across 933 men&apos;s internationals (2002–2026, 756,599 deliveries), Australia average 26.5 in Tests in India against 30–31 elsewhere away and 40.5 at home. They handle the new ball there as well as anywhere; from over 16 the scoring rate falls to 41 per 100 balls and dismissals shift decisively toward lbw, bowled and stumped.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <simple-id uuid='{0F1C41D7-C4B7-48D6-9738-59389914DD63}' />
    </dashboard>
  </dashboards>
